They're definitely useful, but not really essential---most of my
ascensions have been with speed boots, rather than jumping.  At
the point where you are, I'd say that the most important thing
is to advance as fast as possible: you've got enough to go all
the way, and the last thing you want to do is to hang around and
have Rodney appear more often than avoidable.  (Teleporting the
monsters, then advancing with speed boots may not be quite as
fast as jumping, but it's still good enough.)

> So I just wanted to get some opinions as to spend time trying
> to acquire jumping before doing the invocation.

It might have been worth spending a bit of time before killing
the Wizard, but definitely not after.  The only things you
definitly need now are scrolls of gold detection (if you don't
have at least 4 or 5); some cursed scrolls of teleport and some
cursed potions of gain level wouldn't hurt either.  (The first
time I ascended, I went through Moloch's Sanctum the hard way,
but that was as a Valk, twoweaponing a +7 Grayswander and a +6
or +7 katana, so I didn't loose too much time in the graveyard.)

